{"schema": 1, "kind": "review", "id": "rev-20261126T161650Z-d9075ef2", "ts": "2026-11-26T16:23:08Z", "actor": {"worktree": "prawduct", "plugin": "3.10.1-dev", "branch": "fix/fork-project-dir", "build": "41186e401b76"}, "body": {"base_commit": "41186e401b76165bb641fc4acf19eac7e5013a88", "base_tree": "e3cef757e96ace16b5d399ab41e07f9c69dbb43e", "head_tree": "26b1ed9d989b77dee93cac8091dd335f76ce2720", "head_commit": "c0cd5540939ccd76c68c7b009af39a482c5b65b2", "dispatch_commit": "c0cd5540939ccd76c68c7b009af39a482c5b65b2", "mode": "cumulative (bundle review, ready for merge)", "mode_chosen_by": "explicit-args", "stage": "boundary", "tier": "escalate", "roster": [{"role": "correctness", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "design", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}, {"role": "sustainability", "model": "claude-opus-5-5"}], "files_reviewed": ["plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/methodology/delegation.md", "plugin/skills/advisory/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/backlog/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md", "tests/test_project_dir_option.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_changed": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-fork-project-dir.md", ".prawduct/changes/fork-project-dir.md", "plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "plugin/methodology/delegation.md", "plugin/skills/advisory/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/backlog/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md", "tests/test_project_dir_option.py", "tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-fork-project-dir.md", ".prawduct/changes/fork-project-dir.md"], "findings": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "critic SKILL.md still tells a dispatching fork to 'run no consolidate', contradicting coordinator.md's new self-consolidation under --project-dir", "recommendation": "Class: the mid-build coordinator fix (plan 'Coordinator gap') reached coordinator.md step 3 only. SKILL.md step 7 still says, on both dispatch branches, to dispatch and then STOP: line 63 (`reviewer_model` set) 'then **STOP** \u2014 no partial, no consolidate', and line 65 (coordinator roster) 'You write no partial and run no consolidate; there is no resume-to-aggregate.' The fork reads SKILL.md first and those sentences are categorical. A fork that obeys them under a `--project-dir` naming another tree leaves that tree's review unconsolidated. SubagentStop resolves the launch repo from `event.cwd` (cmd_subagent_stop), and the session-end backstop (cmd_stop) also runs in the launch repo, so nothing in the session ever merges the partials. The other tree keeps a live marker and a complete roster, and its next critic-begin refuses with exit 1. Fix it through one owner: make both SKILL.md sentences relational ('\u2026unless --project-dir names another tree: coordinator.md step 3'), or drop them and let coordinator.md own when the fork consolidates. Extend test_the_coordinator_hands_the_tree_to_reviewers_and_consolidates_it so it also fails while SKILL.md says 'no consolidate' with no --project-dir exception. Also state what happens when the harness backgrounds the reviewers and the fork ends before they return: 'once every reviewer returns' then has no one to perform it.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md"], "scope": "class", "closure": "A sentence in a file the critic fork reads that tells it to run no critic-consolidate after dispatching critic-reviewer subagents, with no exception for a --project-dir naming another tree.", "members": [{"id": "m1", "site": "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md:63 (reviewer_model set branch)"}, {"id": "m2", "site": "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md:65 (coordinator roster branch)"}], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "warning", "title": "The skill-level fix for #1253 is verified only at the CLI layer; no fork has been run from a subagent in a second repo", "recommendation": "Goal 2: 'For user-visible changes: product verified beyond tests \u2192 WARNING if no evidence.' The bug was reported at the skill layer: a context: fork skill called by a subagent working in another repo. The tests check the CLI (test_project_dir_option.py) and the presence of grants and prose. They cannot see whether a fork actually carries --project-dir through every hook call, git -C call and Read, whether the composed grants match what the model writes, or whether the coordinator path completes. That composed path is where the builder already found one gap mid-build (SubagentStop), and the finding above is another. Neither the plan, the commits nor the change record carries a trial. This review also shows why the trial needs a fresh session with --plugin-dir: the machine plugin (prawduct-live) rejects `--project-dir` today (`test-status: unknown argument '--project-dir'`). Before closing #1253, run the measured repro once in a fresh session against this branch's plugin: a subagent in repo B invokes /prawduct:critic and /prawduct:backlog with --project-dir B. Record the outcome in the change record. If the trial is deferred until prawduct-live advances, record that deferral rather than closing the issue on CLI evidence.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/backlog/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/advisory/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md"], "scope": "instance", "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "coordinator step 3 makes cross-tree consolidation a judgment under a heading that says stop, and ties it to the coordinator staying alive", "recommendation": "Instance. Why it broke: the SubagentStop hook, the mechanism that let consolidation survive backgrounded reviewers, cannot reach another tree, and the fix replaced it with a model step without restating the step it sits in. Step 3's bold heading still reads 'Stop \u2014 do not resume to aggregate', and the new sentence then asks the coordinator to wait for every reviewer and consolidate, but only 'under a `--project-dir` naming another tree'. Whether the named dir is 'another tree' is a comparison the coordinator has to make for itself, and two coordinators can answer it differently. If one obeys the heading, judges the condition false, or runs `critic-consolidate` before the last partial lands (it no-ops then and nothing triggers it again in that tree), a complete roster sits unmerged in B. The next `critic-begin` there refuses it as a live review, and the Stop backstop runs in the launch repo, so it never fixes this. `critic-consolidate` is idempotent by dispatch id (its docstring), so make the step unconditional whenever `--project-dir` was given. Rename the step so it no longer says stop for that case. Say how the coordinator knows every reviewer has returned, background completion notifications included. Name the fallback for a coordinator that dies first (the builder runs `prawduct-hook critic-consolidate --project-dir <dir>`). Update the pin in `test_the_coordinator_hands_the_tree_to_reviewers_and_consolidates_it` to match.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md", "tests/test_project_dir_option.py"], "scope": "instance", "closure": "The one step in coordinator.md that owns consolidation when the hook cannot reach the reviewed tree.", "members": [{"id": "m1", "site": "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md step 3"}], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "severity": "warning", "title": "delegation.md tells a delegate to pass --project-dir to each /prawduct:* skill, but only the context: fork skills accept it", "recommendation": "Instance. Why it broke: the plan, the change record and the guard test all scope the option to the `context: fork` skills (critic, backlog, advisory), but the one methodology sentence that tells delegates about it says 'each `/prawduct:*` skill'. Inline skills such as `/prawduct:pr`, `/prawduct:janitor` and `/prawduct:doctor` declare no `--project-dir` and their bodies never read it. A delegate working in repo B that follows this sentence passes the flag to `/prawduct:pr` and treats the repo as handled, while that skill's bare `prawduct-hook` and `git` commands run in its own shell, which starts in the launch repo. That is the silent wrong-repo class #1253 closes. Make the sentence relational instead of universal: each `context: fork` skill takes `--project-dir`, and an inline skill runs in the delegate's own shell, so the delegate anchors those commands itself (`git -C`, absolute paths). The fork set is then the one `test_every_forked_skill_accepts_and_passes_project_dir` already pins.", "files": ["plugin/methodology/delegation.md"], "scope": "instance", "closure": "The delegation.md sentence that claims which skills accept --project-dir.", "members": [{"id": "m1", "site": "plugin/methodology/delegation.md \u00a7 Dispatch and reaping, first paragraph"}], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "scope-trace: delegation.md tells a delegate to pass --project-dir to every /prawduct:* skill, but only the three forked skills accept it", "recommendation": "The new sentence in plugin/methodology/delegation.md says a delegate in another repository \"passes `--project-dir <its toplevel>` to each `/prawduct:*` skill\". Only critic, backlog and advisory declare or forward the argument; that is all the change built, and test_every_forked_skill_accepts_and_passes_project_dir pins only `context: fork` skills. Inline skills that drive prawduct-hook (pr: 33 hook references, doctor: 24, report-bug, onboard, janitor, migrate, repo-disable) neither declare it nor tell the agent to append it. The delegate's inline-skill shell also starts in the launch repo, and `resolve_project_dir` honours the launch pin over an unrelated repo at cwd (gitstate.py rule 4). So a delegate that follows the sentence runs `/prawduct:pr --project-dir B` (or doctor), the argument is dropped, and every hook call reads and writes the launch repo's state: the #1253 failure, on skills the methodology now says are covered. Scope: instance. Why it broke: the sentence names the whole skill family, and the change covered only the forked subset. Fix it by naming the forked skills (or 'a `context: fork` skill'), and say that an inline skill's prawduct-hook calls need the option appended directly. The other fix is to extend the argument to the inline skills that call the hook.", "files": ["plugin/methodology/delegation.md"], "check": "scope-trace", "scope": "instance", "closure": "A methodology sentence that promises --project-dir handling for skills that do not implement it.", "members": [{"id": "m1", "site": "plugin/methodology/delegation.md \u00a7 Dispatch and reaping, 'passes `--project-dir <its toplevel>` to each `/prawduct:*` skill'"}], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "severity": "warning", "title": "Backlog and advisory name their store only when --project-dir is given, so a caller that forgot it still gets a silent write into the launch repo", "recommendation": "The plan's decision (build-plan Goals, 'The tree line' bullet) says backlog and advisory writes name their store where they do not already, which pairs with critic's tree line. Its purpose is that a caller who forgot the option can see it. The shipped prose names the store only inside the conditional: backlog SKILL.md 'When the arguments carry `--project-dir <dir>` ... name the file you wrote in your result', and advisory step 2 'when `$ARGUMENTS` carries `--project-dir <dir>`, ... name `<dir>` as the store'. The failure #1253 reports is a subagent in repo B that does NOT pass the option. That subagent still gets 'filed PRAWDUCT-xxxx' or 'dismissed' with no repo named, and the write lands in the launch repo's .prawduct/. Critic surfaces this case through the unconditional tree line, and the two write-path skills have no equivalent, so nothing shows it. Scope: instance. Why it broke: the naming was written into the --project-dir branch instead of the result format. Name the resolved store (its toplevel, or `<dir>/.prawduct/backlog.md` and the advisory store) in every write result, whether or not the option was given.", "files": ["plugin/skills/backlog/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/advisory/SKILL.md"], "scope": "instance", "closure": "A forked write-path skill whose result names its store only when --project-dir was passed.", "members": [{"id": "m1", "site": "plugin/skills/backlog/SKILL.md 'Another repository.' paragraph"}, {"id": "m2", "site": "plugin/skills/advisory/SKILL.md How to use this skill, step 2"}], "fid": "R-6"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 6, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "_apply_project_dir's fail-closed ImportError branch has no test", "recommendation": "The plan records 'Validation fails closed when lib/ will not import, unlike the rest of dispatch' as a decision, and no test drives that branch. Every flow has at least one tested error case and the branch is hard to reach, so this is not rated. A monkeypatched _gitstate raising ImportError, with an assertion of exit 1 and 'Nothing ran.', would pin it cheaply.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook", "tests/test_project_dir_option.py"], "oid": "O-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "title": "'Two different values' compares raw strings, so /x/b and /x/b/ are refused as two trees", "recommendation": "_pop_project_dir compares `given != value` textually before any normalisation. The critic forwards its arguments verbatim and also appends the option, so a caller's trailing slash or a symlinked spelling that the model normalises when appending exits 2 ('names two trees'). The refusal is loud and names both values, so nobody is misled. Comparing os.path.normpath of both values (or Path(...).resolve() after the isabs check) would remove the false refusal if it is wanted.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "oid": "O-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "title": "The manifest's native_review prompt assumes an isolation worktree of the reviewed repo, which `isolation: \"worktree\"` cannot make for a --project-dir naming another repo", "recommendation": "Under --project-dir B, critic-begin writes a native_review prompt naming B. Its dispatcher's `isolation: \"worktree\"` cuts a worktree of the launch repo, and 'prepare' there cannot reach B's commit, so the prompt stops at 'If it exits non-zero, stop'. It fails closed and the plan's scope lists only critic, backlog and advisory. Worth one line in the plan's Out of scope so the paired native review's absence on cross-repo reviews is a recorded choice.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "oid": "O-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "critic-begin now names the reviewed tree twice on the dispatch path", "recommendation": "The new first line, `PRAWDUCT: tree <toplevel> \u00b7 <branch> @ <sha12>`, does exactly what the existing PDT-WT9K line 'PRAWDUCT: reviewing worktree \u2026 branch \u2026 base \u2026 \u2014 confirm this is where the work lives' was added for (its comment: 'surface the resolved target so a wrong-tree review is obvious'). It just does it on every outcome. On dispatch the fork now gets both, in two formats. Consider moving the old line's one extra fact (base) into the new line and deleting the old one. `tests/test_critic_consolidate.py:7438` pins 'reviewing worktree' and would move with it.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "oid": "O-4"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "the backlog skill's --project-dir paragraph tells it to run git as `git -C <dir>`, which it has no grant to run", "recommendation": "The backlog skill's allowed-tools grants no `git` form at all, so the 'run git as `git -C <dir>`' clause tells it to do something it cannot do. Harmless, because the skill runs no git, but the clause can be deleted.", "files": ["plugin/skills/backlog/SKILL.md"], "oid": "O-5"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "the new hook code reaches into gitstate's private helpers", "recommendation": "Class: `prawduct-hook` calls `gitstate._git_toplevel` and `gitstate._git_head_sha` at 7 sites, 3 of them new in `_critic_tree_line` and `_apply_project_dir`. The function that validates `--project-dir` now depends on a helper gitstate does not export. Public `git_toplevel` / `head_sha` names in gitstate would own every caller (grep `gitstate()._\\|gitstate._` in plugin/bin). Not owed in this change.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "oid": "O-6"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "title": "the paired native review is not carried to another tree", "recommendation": "On a development build, `critic-begin` pairs a native review whose wrapper runs `native-review prepare` from an `isolation: \"worktree\"` agent. That worktree belongs to the launch repo, so under `--project-dir` naming a different repository, `prepare` cannot detach it at the reviewed head. The pairing then stops (the wrapper is told to stop on a non-zero exit). Since it is never awaited, the effect is only a missing pairing, but it is worth recording as a known limit or skipping the pairing when the named tree is not the launch repo's repository.", "files": ["plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "oid": "O-7"}, {"goal": "Everything Is Coherent", "title": "the new budget comments repeat one rationale verbatim and cite a 'step 0' that SKILL.md does not number", "recommendation": "In `tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py` the same 7-line +108 rationale appears four times, and the coordinator-round rationale twice. That follows the file's existing convention. 'step 0' in those comments and in test_v5_methodology.py means the unnumbered project-directory paragraph above step 1. Nothing reads either. No edit wanted.", "files": ["tests/test_reviewer_payload_budget.py", "tests/test_v5_methodology.py"], "oid": "O-8"}, {"goal": "The System Can Be Understood", "title": "The coordinator's self-consolidation under --project-dir is prose-only and does not say what to do with consolidation's NEXT-ACTION line", "recommendation": "coordinator.md step 3 now tells the coordinator to run `critic-consolidate --project-dir [dir]` itself once every reviewer returns. It still heads the step 'Stop \u2014 do not resume to aggregate', and it does not say to relay the NEXT-ACTION line, which the single-pass path makes the builder's last line. If the reviewers are backgrounded, the coordinator has already stopped and nothing merges in the other tree; the review then waits on the marker TTL or the complete-roster refusal at the next critic-begin there. The only test is a phrase check on the prose (test_the_coordinator_hands_the_tree_to_reviewers_and_consolidates_it). Consider saying that NEXT-ACTION is relayed on this path.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md"], "oid": "O-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "The plan's design calls are still marked 'inferred, open for the owner at the boundary review', and this is that review", "recommendation": "Every decision in the build plan records its reason, so Goal 5's recorded-why bar is met. Two lists stay owner-unconfirmed: 'Decisions (inferred, mine ...)' and 'Decisions made mid-build (inferred ...)'. The real forks are: refusing a subdirectory rather than walking up; accepting the same value twice; no CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR rewrite for child processes; and coordinator self-consolidation. Surface those to the owner individually before merge. The budget raises and grant shapes can be bulk-confirmed.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-fork-project-dir.md"], "oid": "O-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "title": "Records Pass: the change record leaves out the coordinator round", "recommendation": "Covered set: .prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md, .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-fork-project-dir.md, .prawduct/changes/fork-project-dir.md. No record clears a bar. The api-contract dispatcher-option and tree-line entries, and the change record's refusal and exit-code claims, match `_pop_project_dir`, `_apply_project_dir` and `cmd_critic_begin`. The change record says 'Chunk 01 shipped the whole fix'. It does not mention the follow-up commit c0cd5540: coordinator reviewers carry --project-dir on their probes, and the coordinator consolidates a review in another tree itself. Nothing a consumer does depends on the omission, so no edit is owed.", "files": [".prawduct/changes/fork-project-dir.md"], "oid": "O-11"}], "duration_seconds": 660, "scope": "fork-project-dir", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": ["01"], "chunks_proposed": ["01"], "chunks_declared": false, "chunks_evidence": {"01": {"paths": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/changes/fork-project-dir.md", "plugin/bin/prawduct-hook"], "paths_more": 5, "commits": ["36698108af9d"]}}, "base_reviewed": "41186e401b76165bb641fc4acf19eac7e5013a88", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/api-contract.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-fork-project-dir.md", ".prawduct/changes/fork-project-dir.md", "plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md", "plugin/methodology/delegation.md", "plugin/skills/advisory/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/backlog/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md"], "chunk_graded": "01", "chunks_graded": ["01"], "plan_graded": ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-fork-project-dir.md", "findings": [], "unchecked": [], "counts": {"chunk-ref-missing": 0, "governed-by-gap": 0, "suite-total-claim": 0, "learnings-over-budget": 0, "learnings-budget-unreasoned": 0, "learnings-core-raise-unapproved": 0, "learnings-rule-too-long": 0, "learnings-rule-body": 0, "learnings-area-dead": 0, "change-fragment": 0, "retired-claim-survives": 0, "lat